  isTimeAttack: 0
  timeAttackDuration: 60
  winCondition: 0
  requiredIntactTime: 5
  goldReward: 500
  expReward: 100
  offerDialogue:
    name: Vance
    sentences:
    - Now that you understand tension and compression, let's put that knowledge to
      use.
    - We need a bridge that gives vehicles a shorter route through the canyon.
    - This bridge will connect the factory road to the supply point on the middle
      rock shelf.
    - The crossing is <b><#E09500>80 meters</color></b> wide.
    - The four cargo items you've loaded are part of the test's combined vehicle-and-cargo
      live load.
    - <b><#E09500>As that weight moves across, different parts of the bridge may
      experience tension or compression</color></b>.
    - Pay attention to how the structural members behave during the test.
    - Watch how they work together to support the loaded vehicle.
    - If you're ready, I can give you the contract.
  continueOfferDialogue:
    name: Vance
    sentences: []
  reminderDialogue:
    name: Vance
    sentences:
    - Take your time with the design, {PlayerName}.
    - Keep all four required cargo items on the truck for the test.
    - Remember what we discussed about tension and compression.
    - Keep an eye on how the different parts of the bridge respond when the loaded
      vehicle crosses.
  finishedContractDialogue:
    name: Vance
    sentences:
    - Now that's a shortcut.
    - The loaded vehicle can reach the middle supply point instead of taking the
      long way around the canyon.
    - That should save everyone using this first part of the route a lot of travel
      time.
    - And you've seen how tension and compression affect different parts of a bridge.
    - Well done, {PlayerName}.
    - Let's review what you've learned before you continue the delivery route.
